From: RelicOS <relicos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3326: keep U-Boot away from the SD card rails

On the R36S, U-Boot proper's SD init walks the entire command dialogue
(CMD0..CMD7, ACMD41 reports ready) and then times out on the first data
transfer, ACMD51/SEND_SCR, wedging the controller — with DMA and with
fifo-mode alike. SPL, which does not touch regulators, reads the same
card fine.

Arch-R hit the same failure on mainline U-Boot (their rk3326 handheld
DTS carries the scar: "if u-boot tries to manage these voltages, some
SD cards fail to initialize") and ships the same fix: no vmmc-supply /
vqmmc-supply on &sdmmc, so the mmc core leaves the RK817 rails exactly
as the BootROM left them. Linux manages the rails properly later.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3326-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3326-u-boot.dtsi
index 6503a93..f1a6f0e 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3326-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3326-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -97,6 +97,14 @@
 
 	/* mmc to sram can't do dma, prevent aborts transferring TF-A parts */
 	u-boot,spl-fifo-mode;
+
+	/* R36S: when U-Boot manages the SD rails through the RK817, the
+	 * first data transfer (ACMD51) times out and the controller wedges.
+	 * Arch-R hit the same failure on mainline U-Boot and ships the same
+	 * fix: leave the regulators alone (the kernel manages them fine).
+	 */
+	/delete-property/ vmmc-supply;
+	/delete-property/ vqmmc-supply;
 };
 
 &sdmmc_bus4 {
